amage that would be dealt to this creature by Torrent of Lava this turn."', 'Trample', "Trample; banding (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", "Trample\\nPhasing (This phases in or out before you untap during each of your untap steps. While it's phased out, it's treated as though it doesn't exist.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, all lands you control phase out. (They phase in before you untap during your next untap step.)", 'Trample\\nWhen Phyrexian Dreadnought enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you sacrifice any number of creatures with total power 12 or greater.', 'Trample\\n{1}{G}: Canopy Dragon gains flying and loses trample until end of turn.', 'Tropical Storm deals X damage to each creature with flying and 1 additional damage to each blue creature.', "Uktabi Wildcats's power and toughness are each equal to the number of Forests you control.\\n{G}, Sacrifice a Forest: Regenerate Uktabi Wildcats.", 'Untap target creature an opponent controls and gain control of it until end of turn. That creature gains haste until end of turn. When you lose control of the creature, tap it.', 'Untap target nonattacking creature. It gets +1/+3 until end of turn.', 'Unyaro Bee Sting deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Volcanic Geyser deals X damage to any target.', 'When Auspicious Ancestor dies, you gain 3 life.\\nWhenever a player casts a white spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, you gain 1 life.', 'When Bazaar of Wonders enters the battlefield, exile all graveyards.\\nWhenever a player casts a spell, counter it if a card with the same name is in a graveyard or a nontoken permanent with the same name is on the battlefield.', "When Mangara's Tome enters the battlefield, search your library for five cards, exile them in a face-down pile, and shuffle that pile. Then shuffle your library.\\n{2}: The next time you would draw a card this turn, instead put the top card of the exiled pile into its owner's hand.", 'When Merfolk Seer dies, you may pay {1}{U}. If you do, draw a card.', 'When a spell or ability an opponent controls causes you to discard Sand Golem, return Sand Golem from your graveyard to the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it at the beginning of the next end step.', 'Whenever Brushwagg blocks or becomes blocked, it gets -2/+2 until end of turn.', "Whenever Coral Fighters attacks and isn't blocked, look at the top card of defending player's library. You may put that card on the bottom of that player's library.", "Whenever Crypt Cobra attacks and isn't blocked, defending player gets a poison counter. (A player with ten or more poison counters loses the game.)", 'Whenever Dread Specter blocks or becomes blocked by a nonblack creature, destroy that creature at end of combat.', "Whenever Dream Fighter blocks or becomes blocked by a creature, Dream Fighter and that creature phase out. (While they're phased out, they're treated as though they don't exist. Each one phases in before its controller untaps during their next untap step.)", 'Whenever Goblin Elite Infantry blocks or becomes blocked, it gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Jungle Wurm becomes blocked, it gets -1/-1 until end of turn for each creature blocking it beyond the first.', "Whenever Kukemssa Pirates attacks and isn't blocked, you may gain control of target artifact defending player controls. If you do, Kukemssa Pirates assigns no combat damage this turn.", "Whenever Lead Golem attacks, it doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'Whenever Mtenda Lion attacks, defending player may pay {U}. If that player does, prevent all combat damage that would be dealt by Mtenda Lion this turn.', 'Whenever Rock Basilisk blocks or becomes blocked by a non-Wall creature, destroy that creature at end of combat.', 'Whenever Sabertooth Cobra deals damage to a player, that player gets a poison counter. The player gets another poison counter at the beginning of their next upkeep unless they pay {2} before that step. (A player with ten or more poison counters loses the game.)', 'Whenever Zebra Unicorn deals damage, you gain that much life.', 'Whenever a creature attacks you, it loses flanking until end of turn.\\nWhenever a creature without flying attacks you, Barbed Foliage deals 1 damage to it.', 'Whenever a nontoken creature is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, exile that card.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may pay {4} and 2 life. If you do, return a card exiled with Purgatory to the battlefield.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a spell that targets you or a creature you control, you may draw a card.', "You gain 5 life.\\nWhen a spell or ability an opponent controls causes you to discard Mangara's Blessing, you gain 2 life, and you return Mangara's Blessing from your graveyard to your hand at the beginning of the next end step.", 'You gain X plus 3 life.', "You may cast Armor of Thorns as though it had flash. If you cast it any time a sorcery couldn't have been cast, the controller of the permanent it becomes sacrifices it at the beginning of the next cleanup step.\\nEnchant nonblack creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2.", "You may cast Grave Servitude as though it had flash. If you cast it any time a sorcery couldn't have been cast, the controller of the permanent it becomes sacrifices it at the beginning of the next cleanup step.\\nEnchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +3/-1 and is black.", "You may cast Lightning Reflexes as though it had flash. If you cast it any time a sorcery couldn't have been cast, the controller of the permanent it becomes sacrifices it at the beginning of the next cleanup step.\\nEnchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+0 and has first strike.", "You may cast Soar as though it had flash. If you cast it any time a sorcery couldn't have been cast, the controller of the permanent it becomes sacrifices it at the beginning of the next cleanup step.\\nEnchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +0/+1 and has flying.", "You may cast Ward of Lights as though it had flash. If you cast it any time a sorcery couldn't have been cast, the controller of the permanent it becomes sacrifices it at the beginning of the next cleanup step.\\nEnchant creature\\nAs Ward of Lights enters the battlefield, choose a color.\\nEnchanted creature has protection from the chosen color. This effect doesn't remove Ward of Lights.", "You may choose not to untap Amber Prison during your untap step.\\n{4}, {T}: Tap target artifact, creature, or land. That permanent doesn't untap during its controller's untap step for as long as Amber Prison remains tapped.", 'You may choose not to untap Hivis of the Scale during your untap step.\\n{T}: Gain control of target Dragon for as long as you control Hivis and Hivis remains tapped.', 'You may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield. If you do, sacrifice it unless you pay its mana cost reduced by up to {2}.', "You may tap or untap target artifact, creature, or land.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Zombie Mob enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it for each creature card in your graveyard.\\nWhen Zombie Mob enters the battlefield, exile all creature cards from your graveyard.', "{0}: Mist Dragon gains flying. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)\\n{0}: Mist Dragon loses flying. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)\\n{3}{U}{U}: Mist Dragon phases out. (While it's phased out, it's treated as though it doesn't exist. It phases in before you untap during your next untap step.)", '{1}, Pay 1 life: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{1}, Sacrifice a creature: The next time a source of your choice would deal damage to any target this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}{G}, {T}: Create a 0/1 green Wall creature token with defender named Wood.\\nSacrifice a token named Wood: Add {R}.', '{1}{R}: Reckless Embermage deals 1 damage to any target and 1 damage to itself.', '{1}{R}{R}, {T}: Search your library for a Dragon permanent card, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle. That Dragon gains haste until end of turn. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step.', '{1}{R}{R}: Burning Palm Efreet deals 2 damage to target creature with flying and that creature loses flying until end of turn.', "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Grinning Totem: Search target opponent's library for a card and exile it. Then that player shuffles. Until the beginning of your next upkeep, you may play that card. At the beginning of your next upkeep, if you haven't played it, put it into its owner's graveyard.", '{2}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Draw a card.', "{2}, {T}: Telim'Tor's Darts deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.", '{2}, {T}: The next time a source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage. Exile cards from the top of your library equal to the damage prevented this way.', '{2}, {T}: Until end of turn, target creature you control gains flying and has base toughness 1.', '{2}: Igneous Golem gains trample until end of turn.', '{2}: Raging Spirit becomes colorless until end of turn.', '{2}{R}, {T}: Destroy target nonbasic land.', "{3}, {T}, Tap an untapped creature you control: Unerring Sling deals damage equal to the tapped creature's power to target attacking or blocking creature with flying.", '{3}: Patagia Golem gains flying until end of turn.', '{4}, {T}: Whenever target creature deals combat damage to a non-Wall creature this turn, destroy that non-Wall creature. When the targeted creature leaves the battlefield this turn, sacrifice Acidic Dagger. Activate only before blockers are declared.', '{4}: Sawback Manticore gains flying until end of turn.\\n{1}: Sawback Manticore deals 2 damage to target attacking or blocking creature. Activate only if Sawback Manticore is attacking or blocking and only once each turn.', '{5}, {T}, Exile Amulet of Unmaking: Exile target artifact, creature, or land. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{B}, Pay 1 life: Sewer Rats gets +1/+0 until end of turn. Activate no more than three times each turn.', '{B}, Sacrifice Urborg Panther: Destroy target creature blocking Urborg Panther.\\nSacrifice a creature named Feral Shadow, a creature named Breathstealer, and Urborg Panther: Search your library for a card named Spirit of the Night, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{B}, Sacrifice a Swamp: Put a +1/+1 counter on Mire Shade. Activate only as a sorcery.', "{B}, {T}: Tap target creature. Abyssal Hunter deals damage equal to Abyssal Hunter's power to that creature.", '{B}, {T}: Target creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\n{G}, {T}: Target creature gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', '{B}: Breathstealer gets +1/-1 until end of turn.', '{B}: Fetid Horror gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{B}: Regenerate Restless Dead.', '{B}: Target green creature blocking Barbed-Back Wurm gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', "{B}{R}, {T}: Shauku's Minion deals 2 damage to target white creature.", '{G}, Sacrifice a Forest: Foratog gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', '{G}, {T}, Sacrifice a Forest: Regenerate target creature.', "{G}, {T}: Target creature gets +0/+1 until end of turn.\\n{U}, {T}: Put target creature you control on top of its owner's library.", '{R}, {T}, Sacrifice Flame Elemental: It deals damage equal to its power to target creature.', '{R}, {T}, Sacrifice a Goblin: Red creatures get +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{R}, {T}: Destroy target artifact. That artifact deals damage equal to its mana value to Goblin Tinkerer.', '{R}, {T}: Granger Guildmage deals 1 damage to any target and 1 damage to you.\\n{W}, {T}: Target creature gains first strike until end of turn.', '{R}: Pyric Salamander gets +1/+0 until end of turn. Sacrifice Pyric Salamander at the beginning of the next end step.', '{R}: Regenerate Jungle Troll.\\n{G}: Regenerate Jungle Troll.', '{T}, Sacrifice Daring Apprentice: Counter target spell.', '{T}, Sacrifice a Swamp: Target creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.\\n{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add {U}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Crystal Vein: Add {C}{C}.', "{T}: Destroy target attacking or blocking Dragon. It can't be regenerated. You gain life equal to its power.", '{T}: Femeref Archers deals 4 damage to target attacking creature with flying.', '{T}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', "{T}: Target creature with power 2 or less can't be blocked this turn.", '{T}: Target spell becomes colorless.\\n{T}: Target permanent becomes colorless until end of turn.', '{U}, {T}, Sacrifice Wave Elemental: Tap up to three target creatures without flying.', "{U}, {T}: Put target creature you control on top of its owner's library.\\n{R}, {T}: Shadow Guildmage deals 1 damage to any target and 1 damage to you.", '{W}, {T}: Target creature gains first strike until end of turn.\\n{B}, {T}: Target creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{X}{1}, {T}: Put X charge counters on Ventifact Bottle. Activate only as a sorcery.\\nAt the beginning of your precombat main phase, if Ventifact Bottle has a charge counter on it, tap it and remove all charge counters from it. Add {C} for each charge counter removed this way.']
flavor: ['". . . and when the farmer awoke the next morning, all the seeds from his field were once again in their sacks."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '". . . pirates gambled with a djinn and lost the thing more dear than gold."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"A brilliant light can either illuminate or blind. How will you know which until you open your eyes?"\\n—Asmira, Holy Avenger', '"A treasure to guard other treasures is worth the highest price."\\n—Mtai, Civic Guildmage', '"A vizier\'s dish, best served drenched in honey and almonds."\\n—Suq\'Ata royal recipe', '"A zombie\'s bed must be a lumpy one or he wouldn\'t leave it so often."\\n—Rana, Suq\'Ata market fool', '"Across the plains, farmers who braved the mists began to vanish. Most blamed the goblins; none guessed the truth."\\n—Hakim, Loreweaver', '"After the storm, I found a sea turtle dying on the sands, a blade of grass driven through its shell."\\n—*Travelogue of Najat*', '"Ahh! Opposable digits!"', '"Air hot with sulfur. / Earth heaves beneath me. / Could it be the mountain / ate something bad?"\\n—Dwarven mining song', '"All animals—even humans—can be herded. The trick is to make them think they choose their own destination."\\n—Mangara', '"Amazing thing, gravity. It seems to work every time."\\n—Telim\'Tor', '"An ancient court mage unified the houses into guilds to serve Zhalfir above their own interests. Even during the civil war, the guilds stood together, a testament to the wisdom of Teferi."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"Any day that I ride my horse up to my ankles in the remains of my enemies is a good day."\\n—Akin, seasoned askari', '"As a child, I slept with a cloth over my face, to hide from the spirits that might pull the air from my lungs."\\n—Mosi, Femeref weaver', '"Aselbo soon had the rhino eating from his palm and the snake waiting at his heels."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"Be like the meerkat, my daughters: ever vigilant, true to your own, and wary of strangers."\\n—Nabil Alamat, Suq\'Ata merchant', '"Big one I, One big eye. One-eye see Two-eye die!"\\n—Traditional cyclops chant', '"Blow, fiery wind, / strip illusion from the eye. / Blow, fiery wind of truth."\\n—Femeref chant', '"But I signed nothing!"\\n—Taraneh, Suq\'Ata mage', '"Can they *do* that?"\\n—Imwita, Zhalfirin artificer, last words', '"Can you prepare for the unexpected? No, you cannot. You can prepare only to be surprised."\\n—Teferi', '"Comfortable even in a furnace? I\'ve never met one who\'d accept my wager."\\n—Talibah, embermage', '"Command is the act of balancing on a vine and convincing others that it is firm ground."\\n—Sidar Jabari', '"Common soldiers can\'t understand what a sidar knows: the enemy can be a resource."\\n—Sidar Jabari', '"Consider the wave: how weak the mother yet how strong the child."\\n—Tywanna, Shaper Guildmage', '"Death is not a debt I am yet willing to pay."\\n—Purraj of Urborg', '"Defiantly, the young cyclops popped the brushwagg into his mouth. His cheeks suddenly puffed, his eye bulged, and he was forced to agree with his elder."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"Do not go there, do not go / unless you rise on wings, unless you walk on hooves."\\n—"Song to the Sun," Femeref song', '"Dragonfire forged me a warrior."\\n—Rashida Scalebane', '"Enchant me with your tale-telling. Tell about Tree, Grass, River, and Wind. / Tell why Truth must fight with Falsehood, and why Truth will always win."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"Eternal life or your money back."\\n—Unnamed Suq\'Ata merchant, deceased', '"Even the ancient storytellers proclaimed Zhalfir to be dominant over all Jamuraa. Kaervek\'s invasion shocked us all."\\n—Hakim, Loreweaver', '"Execution awaits the dissenter."\\n—Kasib ibn Naji, *Letters*', '"Faith is my shield, and hope is my armor; I am vulnerable only to myself."\\n—Asmira, Holy Avenger', '"Femeref was guided by the wisdom of the Council of Voices. But in one terrible instant, they were slain, leaving Asmira as the sole voice of leadership."\\n—Hakim, Loreweaver', '"Fetch the pestridder, Paka—we\'ve got dwarves in the rutabagas!"\\n—Jamul, Femeref farmer', '"Frozen, we watched the funnel pluck up three of the goats—pook! pook! pook!—before we ran for the wadi."\\n—*Travelogue of Najat*', '"Heel."', '"Her beauty was the beauty of the Sun at midday, deadly to those who underestimated her strength."\\n—Azeworai, "Kenechi\'s Dream"', '"Hmmm—midnight snack."', '"How ironic that the greatest forge of civilization is battle."\\n—Mangara', '"I dance the nothing dance, / Feet in the air, knives in the ground."\\n—Femeref chant', '"I do not teach. I simply reveal."\\n—Daudi, Femeref tutor', '"I don\'t know what takes them; they die around me without time to scream."\\n—Scout Ekemet, final journal', '"I hate insects of every sort. The only mercy is that they are generally small."\\n—Mwani, Mtenda goatherd', '"I have hidden from the machinations of Zhalfir for centuries. Why should I join *your* campaign?"\\n—Jolrael', '"I no longer believe in a final resting place."\\n—Shauku, Endbringer', '"I see a great victory and rivers of blood. And . . . hmm, looks like a spleen."\\n—Grishnak, goblin soothsayer', '"I shall make walls of their flesh, and their blood will be my mortar."\\n—Kaervek', '"I will return / with lizard skins for your sandals. Paint your eyes black and wait for me."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"I will tell my father\'s stories . . . . How the elephants trampled the leopard cub, and its father, though he knew, killed nine goats instead."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"I\'ll capture gentle zebras / for your steeds and fill the stable with every kind of unicorn."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"I\'ve never *heard* growth before."\\n—Gowon, Femeref herder', '"If I have learned anything as a wizard it is this: never fight your own battles."\\n—Waffa, sorcerer of Nyomba', '"If it is weak, either kill it or ignore it. Anything else honors it."\\n—Kaervek', '"If magic is your crutch, cast it aside and learn to walk without it."\\n—Teferi', '"If the curse does not strike you dead, question your soul."\\n—Kaervek', '"If the griffins tell of their gods, perhaps they speak of feathers bright as the Sun."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"If you weren\'t born with it, you don\'t need it."\\n—Grahilah, former trader of Amiqat', '"In all my years I\'ve only met one mage who successfully trapped a djinn—and none who tried and failed."\\n—Talibah, embermage', '"In the Mwonvuli you must divide your attention between what hangs overhead and what lies underfoot."\\n—Sidar Jabari', '"In the forest, fires light the sky as black clouds unfold their weight."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"In your final breath you still have something to offer Phyrexia."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"Inhale. Kill. Exhale."', '"It is terrible how one brief action can live forever in memory."\\n—Jolrael', '"It\'s filthy work, planting them."\\n—Kifimbo, Shadow Guildmage', '"Its burning power is more elusive than shade on the Unyaro Plains, more perilous than the horn of a rhino."\\n—Akin, seasoned askari', '"Let him be imprisoned while his possessions wander free."\\n—Suq\'Ata legal decree', '"Life for life: this is the immutable law."\\n—Panya, Granger Guildmage', '"Life is a resource that should belong only to the strong."\\n—Shauku, Endbringer', '"Like Day from Night, / I\'ll live my life apart from you, just glimpsing you across the sky, / because you cannot change, my dear, and nor can I."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"Magic\'s only part of it, my friend. Diet does the rest."\\n—Pashad ibn Asim, Suq\'Ata trader', '"Mangara is gone. Who among you doubts that I have taken his power?"\\n—Kaervek', '"More armies have been lost in the confusion of the jungle mists than to any battle."\\n—Jolrael', '"Much can be learned from the bees about dying for a cause."\\n—Asmira, Holy Avenger', '"My goat was a small price to pay for the chance to see the hunting griffin dive and seize it."\\n—Pashad ibn Asim, Suq\'Ata trader', '"My minions serve me in the light; I serve no one."\\n—Shauku, Endbringer', '"My shield will bear a shining sun so you will always be with me. / Inlaid with gold, it will shine like glowing embers."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"Never taunt an embermage, \'What are you going to do about it?\'"\\n—Akin, seasoned askari', '"Of the six who went down the Uuserk Trail to scout ahead, one returned. She clawed at her eyes and nostrils and sobbed with horror. I was curious about what she saw, but we chose another path."\\n—Scout Ekemet, final journal', '"Omens lie in this early harvest\'s fruit."\\n—Asmira, Holy Avenger', '"Once, a Quirion asked why I was so cautious when the day was clear. I told him of the sky-blue hide of the cerluean wyvern, and he offered me double if I could conjure a strong tailwind!"\\n—Sisay, Captain of the *Weatherlight*', '"Once, a wealthy king commissioned an artificial creature to be crafted from the royal treasury, thinking it a clever ploy to have the jewels guard themselves."\\n—Azeworai, "The Golem\'s Wish"', '"One moment I was walking along the beach, and the next I was high in the air, staring into a hideous smiling face."\\n—Tarub, Suq\'Ata sailor', '"One timely cry of warning can save nine of surprise."\\n—Sidar Jabari', '"Only a gargoyle would take such delight in a thunderstorm."\\n—Qhattib, Vizier of Amiqat', '"Only fools believe they will face my armies but once."\\n—Kaervek', '"Our guardian levies a tax on all traders. Wise travelers pay with a minimum of fuss."\\n—Qhattib, Vizier of Amiqat', '"Our soldiers are blessed with lizard scales as hard and cold as steel."\\n—Sidar Jabari', '"Pathetic—like I wouldn\'t know a goblin painted up to look like a dwarf!"\\n—Pashad ibn Asim, Suq\'Ata trader', '"People laughed at my darts—once."\\n—Telim\'Tor', '"Politics is a game—move a stone here, move a stone there—except sometimes the stones bleed."\\n—Shauku, Endbringer', '"Prophecy is whatever one makes of it, but destiny cannot be changed."\\n—Sidar Jabari', '"Proud am I, / strong am I, / courageous in defending my children / and fierce in punishing what stands in my way."\\n—"So the Elephant Speaks," Zhalfirin song', '"Quick, Rhirhok—teach me to swim!"\\n—Makht, goblin casualty', '"Shadimir was as surprised as he was relieved when the blow turned aside."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"Since I cannot stop death, I choose to stop life."\\n—Kaervek', '"Sorry I burned down your village. Here\'s some gold."', '"Stepping through time is like riding a camel. It may get you where you want to go, but the ride is rarely pleasant."\\n—Teferi', '"Sun follows Moon until she tires, then carries her until she\'s strong / and runs ahead of him again."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"Suq\'Ata believe in trade; Femeref, alms; Zhalfirins, steel. Be warned, Kaervek—now we are joined."\\n—Sidar Jabari', '"Taniwha rolls in its sleep, and the land is awash with the waves."\\n—Poetics of Hanan', '"Tell me . . . have you ever sung the Song of Blood?"\\n—Purraj of Urborg', '"The Burning Isles are the home to a dozen lords who claim dominion. Jamuraa will look to only one leader: me."\\n—Kaervek', '"The Femeref look only to the Sun for healing; they have never truly understood life\'s cycle."\\n—Kifimbo, Shadow Guildmage', '"The Mwonvuli Jungle has given the darkness teeth for tearing the gift of life from the weak."\\n—Jolrael', '"The caliph was so intelligent he could not remember what he knew."\\n—Azeworai, "Three Riddles"', '"The ceremony ended with a voice from the shadows, a voice with vast, ominous power."\\n—Kifimbo, Shadow Guildmage', '"The creature rose from the mountain, its body weeping fire."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"The curious merely amass knowledge. The ambitious use it."\\n—Telim\'Tor', '"The days before the war were filled with strange portents: scouts and herders spoke of villages reduced to ash, of farmers taken from their fields, and of foul beasts roaming the plains in packs. I know, for I spoke to them all."\\n—Hakim, Loreweaver', '"The efreet is a striding storm with a voice that crackles like fire."\\n—Qhattib, Vizier of Amiqat', '"The few of us who survived were denied entry to our camp for two days—so like the pox were the marks we bore."\\n—*Travelogue of Najat*', '"The finest offering of night is not stealth but daring."\\n—Tetlok, Breathstealer', '"The flesh is a casket for the soul."\\n—Shauku, Endbringer', '"The foul entities of the Uuserk swamp had never before dared to spread their influence to the very heart of Zhalfir."\\n—Hakim, Loreweaver', '"The fury in the lion\'s eye;\\nthe patience in the hippo\'s yawn;\\nthe pride within the griffin\'s cry\\nare one within the iron tusk\'s stride."\\n—"Iron Tusk," Femeref song', '"The hazerider danced in the thunderstorm and sang to its music."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"The lion drank that lake right up! In thanks, he gave Siti the power to speak with lions and make them leave the goats alone."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"The memory of your existence will fade like the final stars of morning."\\n—Kaervek', '"The night stalkers are such a minor power in Urborg. Their sad eagerness to elevate themselves makes them willing tools in the plundering of little Femeref."\\n—Kaervek', '"The people wiped the sand from their eyes and cursed—and left the barren land to the hyenas and vipers."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"The protection offered comes at a price. How numerous are your kin?"\\n—Purraj of Urborg', '"The secrets of Phyrexia are expensive. You will pay in brass and bone, steel and sinew."\\n—Kaervek', '"The trollish game of push-fall inspired this impressive tactic."\\n—Sidar Jabari', '"There are harsher ways to learn the meaning of the word \'no.\'"\\n—Rashida Scalebane', '"There are times solid ground gives precious little comfort."\\n—Talibah, embermage', '"There is no sweeter music than the wails of a dying dragon."\\n—Rashida Scalebane', '"There\'s nothing like a sudden shock to clarify one\'s thoughts."\\n—Pashad ibn Asim, Suq\'Ata trader', '"They exist only so long as the living take no notice."\\n—Kifimbo, Shadow Guildmage', '"They knew Bantau was lost when, to hide the pearl he had found on the beach, he swallowed it—and soon grew wings."\\n—Hakim, Loreweaver', '"They say a Zhalfirin archer can split the eye of a griffin. Nonsense, of course: they have no faith to guide their darts."\\n—Nuru, Femeref archer', '"To pass through the jungle: silence, courtesy, ferocity, as the occasion demands."\\n—Kamau, "Proper Passage"', '"To the tutors, a \'poem of sand\' was of little account, a \'poem of ivory,\' priceless."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"To the undiscerning eye, justice and vengeance can look the same."\\n—Rashida Scalebane', '"Tonight we\'ll eat a farewell feast. Cold corn porridge is not enough. / Let\'s peel papayas, pineapples, and mangoes, drink coconut milk, / and bake bananas."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"Turn your back for a second and they just vanish! As if they weren\'t shifty enough before."\\n—Rhirhok, goblin archer', '"Unlike Zhalfir, the griffin needs no council to keep harmony among its parts."\\n—Asmira, Holy Avenger', '"Useful . . . if you can find it."\\n—Pashad ibn Asim, Suq\'Ata trader', '"Water is like breathing—necessary for life."\\n—Asmira, Holy Avenger', '"We realized the bog had not given up a soul but had come to claim a new one."\\n—Scout Ekemet, final journal', '"We threw dried fruit to the drakes that rode the air, streaming along the *Weatherlight\'*s side as we sailed amidst the clouds."\\n—Sisay, Captain of the *Weatherlight*', '"We\'ve run aground sandbars before, but today, a sandbar ran aground us."\\n—Kipkemboi, Kukemssa pirate', '"Wear the falcon\'s feathers in your hair—\\nbe fast as the falcon, bright as the Sun."\\n—"Rise on Wings," Zhalfirin song', '"What is taking them so long to fill the waterskins?"\\n—Mwani, Mtenda goatherd', '"What need have I for cavalry when I can have horse and rider both in one?"\\n—Jolrael', '"What rainbow could possibly come of this rain?"\\n—Asmira, Holy Avenger', '"What you call decay, I call ripening. You\'ll gain no sustenance from this harvest."\\n—Kaervek', '"When traveling the Great Desert avoid wearing the scales of lizards, for the Viashino rule the sands and look poorly on the skinning of their cousins."\\n—*Zhalfirin Guide to the Desert*', '"When we\'re aloft, I love to lean over the *Weatherlight*\'s railing and watch the patterns the griffins\' shadows make on the clouds below."\\n—Sisay, Captain of the *Weatherlight*', '"Whoa—my tail will *never* fit through that hole!"', '"Would you give up your hands to fly? That is what the birds have done."\\n—*The One Thousand Questions*', '"You eat plants; I eat plants. You eat beasts; I eat you."\\n—Drulvurg, troll king', '"You returned a warrior. . . . Your hair was cut, your eye tattooed with the red triangle of war."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', 'A cage may keep you in, but it does not keep the stones out.', 'A crash of rhinos in my head\\n—Femeref expression meaning "a severe head pain"', "A dwarf's life belongs as much to the land as to the dwarf.\\n—Creed of the Stonethrow Clan", 'A hefty price is no guarantee of quality merchandise.', 'A lie always returns; be careful how you catch it.', 'Better a fierce thunderhead than a sky filled with locusts.', "Better to fight the sand for a few hours than to sleep beneath it forever.\\n—Suq'Ata truism", 'Broad as a baobab—and about as smart.', 'Centuries ago, Mangara won the loyalty of the Quirion not by ruling their minds but by supporting their independence.', 'Discovered by Femeref mages, the Null Chamber is the ultimate testing ground for the uncreative.', "Don't insult a Talruum unless your mount is swift.\\n—Suq'Ata saying", "Dreams' riches are easily spent.\\n—Suq'Ata adage", 'Embrace the Harbinger\\n—Suq\'Ata expression meaning "abandon hope"', 'Eternal life brings eternal hunger.', 'Even the lion envies the lark.', 'Even wurms start out small.', 'Facets of life, reflections of the soul.', 'Few are able to underestimate the hordes.', 'Five hundred years to grow—barely a minute to eat.', 'For the first time in his life, Grakk felt a little warm and fuzzy inside.', 'From jungle to sea, from sea to stone, from stone to field, from field to bone. What am I?\\n—Zhalfirin riddle', "From you to me, so me to you.\\n—Femeref children's taunt", 'Good help is hard to dig up.', 'Grieve for the soul in death dishonored.\\n—Shadow Guild saying', 'Held in the lion\'s eye\\n—Zhalfirin saying meaning "caught in the moment of crisis"', 'Hyenas laughing—what\'s the joke?\\n—Femeref phrase meaning "that\'s not funny"', 'I live without food, stand without leg, wound without force, and am harder to fight than to kill. What am I?\\n—Femeref riddle', 'In front of every great wizard is a doomed apprentice.', 'In the Jamuraan jungles, there is often no separating beauty from danger.', 'In the eastern reaches of Jamuraa are arrangements of massive stones. No one knows their origins—for certain.', 'It is not by the blood of dragons that Rashida measures victories, but by the sum of children who no longer wake from nightmares of scales and fire.', 'It scattered falcons like a lion hunting among jackals.', "It's good to know more about your enemy's fate than your enemy does.", 'King or herder, the maggots care not.', 'Leave no mouth agape, no stomach unfilled.\\n—Granger Guild maxim', 'Life and death are two faces of the same coin.', 'Light creates shadow; light destroys shadow. Such is the transience of darkness.', 'Like a laughing knife, immaculate and sharp, is the Melesse.', 'Like some foul herdbeast, it grazes on the dead.', 'Love is like a rhino, short-sighted and hasty; if it cannot find a way, it will make a way.\\n—Femeref adage', 'Made you look.', 'Many mages have been consumed by their work.', 'My thunder comes before the lightning; my lightning comes before the clouds; my rain dries all the land it touches. What am I?\\n—Femeref riddle', 'No two see the same Maro.', 'Not only the sleeping should fear dreams.', 'Only those who have nothing have nothing to fear.', 'Pass me from soul to soul / soldier to herder, herder to beast, beast to soil / until I am everywhere. / Then pass me those souls.\\n—Totem inscription (translated)', "Shape this world in Zhalfir's image.\\n—Shaper Guild maxim", 'Slow and heavy swings the club.', 'Some smiles show cheer; some merely show teeth.', 'Sometimes the wise ones wove their magic into living plants; as the plant grew, so grew the magic.', 'Speed and fire are always a deadly combination.', 'Storyteller: By my hand in the fire, this story is a tale of power. Listeners: May it give you strength.', "Telim'Tor could no longer recall the exact number of assaults—but his troops could.", "The best use for a unicorn's horn is to adorn a unicorn.\\n—Femeref adage", 'The fire breathes while the air burns.', 'The first of the Thousand Deaths.', "The griffin's shadow gives courage to the righteous and dread to the idle.", "The mountain's voice shouts us all down.", "The pulsing heat of the midday Sun burns in the Lion's eye.\\n—Stone inscription, source unknown", "The rich's heirs often thank them after death . . . but preferably not in person.\\n—Suq'Ata epigram", 'The sea leaves no room for tears.\\n—Zhalfirin adage', 'The three wizards knew only that this isle held a great mystery—and that patience alone would solve it.', 'The trees have ears, eyes, and teeth.', "There are medicines for all afflictions but idleness.\\n—Suq'Ata saying", 'There is only so much a person may be buried with.', 'They talk a good fight.', 'Thus does nature assert herself.', "Time is the one shackle you can't break.\\n—Zhalfirin aphorism", "To buy unseen land, pay in unseen coin.\\n—Suq'Ata maxim", 'To condemn the innocent you must first condemn yourself.\\n—Civic Guild maxim', 'To keep the dead so others may live.\\n—Shadow Guild maxim', "Trade to trade, not to keep.\\n—Suq'Ata motto", 'Victim of the two-toed faerie\\n—Suq\'Ata expression meaning "broken"', 'Want all, lose all.\\n—Zhalfirin aphorism', 'Watching the windreaper\\n—Zhalfirin phrase meaning "daydreaming"', 'Whatever follows life is incurable.\\n—Zhalfirin aphorism', 'When mountains ride the sea, waves live upon the fields.', 'When the other soldiers of Zhalfir fall, the askaris will yet stand.', "When you've been chased by a dragon, you run from every lizard.\\n—Suq'Ata saying", "You lie down with rats, and the rats run away.\\n—Suq'Ata insult", "Zhalfir's destiny rings in tempered steel.\\n—Armorer Guild maxim"]
artist: ['Adam Rex', 'Adrian Smith', 'Al Davidson', 'Alan Rabinowitz', 'Andrew Robinson', 'Bob Eggleton', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Charles Gillespie', 'Chippy', 'Cliff Nielsen', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'Dan Frazier', 'David A. Cherry', 'David Ho', "David O'Connor", 'Dermot Power', 'Dom!', 'Donato Giancola', 'Douglas Shuler', 'Drew Tucker', 'Gary Leach', 'Geofrey Darrow', 'Gerry Grace', 'Greg Simanson', 'Hannibal King', 'Harold McNeill', 'Ian Miller', 'Janine Johnston', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Jennifer Law', 'Jock', 'John Avon', 'John Bolton', 'John Coulthart', 'John Malloy', 'John Matson', 'Junior Tomlin', 'Kaja Foglio', 'Kari Johnson', 'Kathryn Rathke', 'Kev Walker', 'Liz Danforth', 'Margaret Organ-Kean', 'Mark Poole', 'Martin McKenna', 'Mike Dringenberg', 'Mike Kerr', 'Mike Kimble', 'Pat Lewis', 'Pete Venters', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Richard Kane Ferguson', 'Richard Thomas', 'Robert Bliss', 'Roger Raupp', 'Ron Spencer', 'Scott Kirschner', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Steve Luke', 'Steve White', 'Stuart Beel', 'Stuart Griffin', 'Susan Van Camp', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Thomas Gianni', 'Tom Kyffin', 'Tom Wänerstrand', 'Tony Roberts', 'Una Fricker', 'William Donohoe', 'Zak Plucinski', 'Zina Saunders']
